# --- Maintainer test harness ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Two clones of FIRST's own repo (~300 MB each) plus the fixtures and setup script that wire Flux
# into them. This is how Flux is verified against the real SDK; no team ever runs it, so it is kept
# locally for the same reason scripts/ is. Anything a test needs on a fresh clone must live in that
# module's own src/test/resources -- see SourceFieldWriterTest.fixtureCopy().
test-ftc-project/

# --- Build output -------------------------------------------------------------------------
build/
out/
# Eclipse-style output directory. IDE Java/Kotlin tooling writes here instead of build/, and it
# copies sources next to the .class files, so without this a clean tree shows ~6500 lines of
# duplicated .kt that *.class below does not catch.
bin/
.gradle/
*.class
*.jar
!gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar

# The published artifact folder IS committed -- it is how teams consume Flux until there is a
# real remote (docs/design/distribution.md). Without these exceptions the *.jar rule above would
# silently drop the very files teams need.
!maven/**/*.jar
!maven/**/*.aar
!maven/**/*.pom
!maven/**/*.module
*.apk
*.dex

# --- Machine-specific ---------------------------------------------------------------------
local.properties
.env

# --- IDE ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws

# --- OS -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Internal design/research notes. Kept locally, deliberately not published.
docs/

# Maintainer-only release tooling. Teams consume artifacts from maven/; they never run this.
scripts/
